# A whole second copy of Ripple, generated so somebody can run and look at the
# finished shape before building it by hand. Every file in it is copied from
# Codebase, so committing it would be a second copy of the product that drifts
# from the first. Two tools write it and it holds whichever ran last:
# tools/make_build_folder.py for the kit-shaped one started with a batch file,
# tools/make_demo_snapshot.py for the one that runs where nothing can be
# installed. Deleting it costs one command. See "never commit a build artefact".
RIPPLE COPILOT DEMO/
